id: tornado-attack
name: Tornado Attack
uaType: technical
prerequisite: Agility Score of 6+
tpCost: 12
type: standard
actionCost: 2
kiCostPerTier: 4
# "You begin Spinning until the start of your next turn" - the Spinning mark on your clock (Dodge 1(T), Damage
# Reduction your Agility Modifier); missed or dealt 0 Damage by an Opponent's attack, a Basic Attack at them out of
# sequence offered on its card (Launching, Sweeping or Elemental (Wind)); starting your next turn with Opponents in your
# Melee Range, a card with the Thrust out of sequence at one of them before it stops (chat.mjs postTornado,
# tornadoTurnStart).
tornado: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Spinning until the start of your next turn: Dodge 1(T) higher, Damage taken lower by your Agility Modifier; missed or
  unharmed by an attack, a Basic Attack back; your next turn begins with a Thrust at an Opponent in reach.
text: >
  Tornado Attack: You spin in place, generating a cyclone of wind around you.
  –Ability Type: Technical
  –Prerequisites: Agility Score of 6+
  –TP Cost: 12
  –KP Cost: 4(T)
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 2 Actions
  –Minions: N/A
  –Passive Bonus: N/A
  –Effect: You begin Spinning until the start of your next turn. While you are Spinning, increase your Dodge Rolls by
  1(T) and reduce all Damage you take by your Agility Modifier. If an Opponent misses you with an Attacking Maneuver or
  deals 0 Damage to you with an Attacking Maneuver, you may use the Basic Attack Maneuver as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.
  If you do, you must target that Opponent with that Attacking Maneuver and you must select either the Launching,
  Sweeping, or Elemental (Wind) Profile for that Attacking Maneuver.

  If you start your next turn while Spinning with an Opponent within your Melee Range, before you stop Spinning, use the
  Thrust Maneuver against that Opponent as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.
